\label{1.1}
Let $N$ be a compact K\"{a}hler manifold with K\"{a}hler metric $h$ and the associated form $\Omega$. Let $f:{\mathbb{A}}(R_0)\rightarrow N$ be a holomorphic curve from annulus ${\mathbb{A}}(R_0)\ (R_0>1)$ into $N$ and let $\omega\in H^{0}(N, \mathcal U^1_N)$. Setting $f^{*}\omega =\xi (z)dz$, we have
$$ \bigl\|\ m_0(r,\xi )\le O\left(\log^+ T_{0,f}(r, \Omega )\right)+O\left(\log^+\frac{1}{R_0-r}\right).$$

\label{1.2}
Let $f:{\mathbb{A}}(R_0)\rightarrow M$ be an algebraically non-degenerate holomorphic curve into a semi-Abelian variety $M$ and let $D$ be a reduced divisor on $M$. Then there exist a smooth equivariant compactification $\overline M$ of $M$ independent of $f$ and a natural number $k_0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\bigl\|\ T_{0,f}(r; c_1(\overline D)) &= N_0^{[k_0]}(r, f^*D)+O\left (\log^+T_{0,f}(r; c_1(\overline D))+\log^+\frac{1}{R_0-r}\right).
\end{align*}

\label{3.1}
Let $f$ be a nonzero multiplicative meromorphic function on ${\mathbb{A}} (R_0)$. Then for each positive integer $k$ and positive number $\epsilon$, we have
$$\biggl\|\ m_0\left (r,\dfrac{f'}{f}\right)\le (4+\epsilon)\log^+T_0(r,f)+O\left(\log^+\frac{1}{R_0-r}\right). $$

\label{10.1}
Let $M$ be a semi-Abelian variety and let $D$ be an algebraic divisor on $M$ such that $\mathrm{St}(D)=\{0\}$.
Then there exists a smooth equivariant compactification $\overline M$ of $M$ such that the closure $\overline D$ of $D$ in $\overline M$ is big, generally positioned.

\label{new4.53} There exists a number $k_0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
\pi_2\big (J_{k_0}(\overline D, \log \partial M)\big )\cap \pi_2(\overline{J_{k_0}f({\mathbb{A}}(R_0) )}^{\mathrm{Zar}})\not= \pi_2(\overline{J_{k_0}f({\mathbb{A}}(R_0) )}^{\mathrm{Zar}}),
\end{align*}
where $\overline{J_{k_0}f({\mathbb{A}}(R_0) )}^{\mathrm{Zar}}$ is the Zariski closure of $J_{k_0}f({\mathbb{A}}(R_0) )$ in $J_k(\overline M, \log \partial M)$.
